Apple's iOS 27.2 and iPadOS 27.2 updates fix more than 160 security vulnerabilities, which means it's a good idea to install the software as soon as you can.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1038581" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/03/apple-lock-security-bug-vulnerability-fix-privacy.jpg" alt="" width="2016" height="1134" /><br/>
An <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> vulnerability that could let a remote attacker access sensitive data was fixed, as was a Hide My Email bug that could leak the user's real email address. There are more than 30 WebKit fixes, and approximately 15 kernel bugs have been addressed.<br/>
<br/>
Six CVEs credit Calif, the team that <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/23/iphone-duo-jailbreak/">jailbroke the iPhone Duo</a> on launch day and demonstrated an untethered iOS 27.0.1 jailbreak. Calif researcher Stefan Esser recently said that "most" of the vulnerabilities used for its jailbreak are fixed in iOS 27.2.<br/>
<br/>
Apple did not say any of the flaws are known to be actively exploited, but with details published, devices that are not updated could be subject to attack.<br/>
<br/>
The number of security fixes in iOS updates <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/04/aple-bug-bounty-limits-ai/">continues to grow</a> as AI models have gotten better at locating vulnerabilities. Anthropic Research is credited on three fixes, and four cite OpenAI.<br/>
<br/>
